00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.668
-So it wasn't even
during the sketch.

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.736
-No. I think Jason Bateman
was the host.

00:09:31.736 --> 00:09:34.440
-Oh, yeah, was it monkeys
throwing poop at celebrities?

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.908
-That's right.
-Yeah.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:39.378
-And I walked by,
and it made eye contact with me,

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.213
and it was like --
And it came out of nowhere

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.115
and grabbed my hand,
and it wouldn't let me go.

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:45.317
-I remember it kept shaking
its head shot at you.

00:09:45.317 --> 00:09:47.653
'Cause he wanted --
-That's right!

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:50.056
-He wanted to meet your agent.
-Yeah.

00:09:50.056 --> 00:09:52.891
And I was like,
"I can't help you."

00:09:52.891 --> 00:09:55.628
Yeah. So maybe I -- You know --

00:09:55.628 --> 00:09:57.930
I have great respect
for animals.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.199
And I don't think anyone or any
sunglasses should go near them.

00:10:01.199 --> 00:10:04.403
-No. I feel no peace
when I'm in a room with --

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:05.771
-No.
-I --

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.140
We don't have animals
on this show anymore.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.408
-Really?

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:11.376
-Because there was a sloth
on the show.

00:10:11.376 --> 00:10:13.111
And I was looking
at the sloth --

00:10:13.111 --> 00:10:14.479
And it was wonderful.
-Yes.

00:10:14.479 --> 00:10:17.515
-I mean, again, it -- You know,
seeing a sloth up close.

00:10:17.515 --> 00:10:19.518
It was a sloth, right?

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.320
And at some point I was
just looking at the sloth,

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.522
and I feel like
we made eye contact.

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:26.692
And what I read from the sloth
was him saying,

00:10:26.692 --> 00:10:27.926
"I don't like it here."

00:10:27.926 --> 00:10:29.428
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:31.764
-Yes. I feel bad for them.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:34.566
-And I think they had told him

00:10:34.566 --> 00:10:36.301
it was a different
late-night show.

00:10:36.301 --> 00:10:37.836
-[Bleep]

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:40.272
-Like, I think it was dawning
on him that this wasn't --

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:42.141
-He was like, "Oh, this isn't
what I thought it was."

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:44.009
He was like, "'Late Night'?

00:10:44.009 --> 00:10:45.644
Oh. I thought it was
a different late night.

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:49.281
-He goes, "I thought it was
the genre of late-night shows.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:51.984
I didn't realize it was
'Late Night,' like, in quotes."

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:55.854
-Yeah. Yeah. Well, then --
-He was look-- He was very slow.

00:10:55.854 --> 00:10:57.956
Again, slowly.
He was looking for The Roots.

00:10:57.956 --> 00:10:59.692
But it was like this.

00:10:59.692 --> 00:11:02.495
[ Laughter ]

00:11:02.495 --> 00:11:04.162
-Yeah.

00:11:04.162 --> 00:11:07.032
-And you could tell, and
that really hurt my feelings.

00:11:07.032 --> 00:11:09.234
I guess it's not really that --
I stopped doing it because I --

00:11:09.234 --> 00:11:12.871
It was very hard to have
my feelings hurt by an animal.

00:11:12.871 --> 00:11:14.540
-Well -- Yeah.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.041
-Hey, a fish
with human-looking teeth

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:17.743
was caught off the coast
of North Carolina.

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:19.512
-I don't buy it.
I don't think that's real.

00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:21.780
-Really? Have you
really not seen this photo?

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.016
-No. This is a real photo?
-Yeah.

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:26.251
Will you be honest...
-Yeah, I'm gonna -- Okay.

00:11:26.251 --> 00:11:28.320
-...if you think this fish
has human-looking teeth?

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.955
-Yes, of course.
-Be honest right away.

00:11:29.955 --> 00:11:32.191
-That's what it's about --
being honest.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:33.792
Hmm...

00:11:33.792 --> 00:11:35.293
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.293 --> 00:11:36.795
It feels like horse teeth.

00:11:36.795 --> 00:11:38.831
-I think it is more horse teeth
than human teeth.

00:11:38.831 --> 00:11:40.532
I agree with you.
-What else do we have?

00:11:40.532 --> 00:11:42.902
-TikTok.
You engage with TikTok.

00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:44.336
You love it.
-I do love it.

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:46.905
-We've talked about it. And
I will admit that I am not --

00:11:46.905 --> 00:11:49.208
-I'm too old for TikTok,
I think, but I love it.

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:51.010
-So people are eating
frozen honey.

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.611
Have you seen this yet?
-That is not on my FYP.

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:56.815
My FYP is very --
-When you eat frozen honey,

00:11:56.815 --> 00:11:59.584
it guess it maybe
gives you diarrhea.

00:11:59.584 --> 00:12:02.221
-And why are they eating it?
Just to see what happens?

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:04.390
-I guess to see what happens.
-To get diarrhea.

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.058
-No, I think the diarrhea
is like, "Uh-oh."

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:07.893
-But why were they eating it
in the first place?

00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:09.761
Just 'cause why not?
-You're on TikTok.

00:12:09.761 --> 00:12:11.296
Hold on. Let me see.

00:12:11.296 --> 00:12:13.098
-Let's see what it says.

00:12:13.098 --> 00:12:14.533
Because that is --
that is specific.

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:16.302
-Guy squeezed a frozen bottle
with both hands.

00:12:16.302 --> 00:12:18.203
Watching the golden goop
come out like toothpaste.

00:12:18.203 --> 00:12:20.772
Then he took a big sticky --
-Okay, so it's an ASMR thing

00:12:20.772 --> 00:12:22.841
where they're like,
"Check how cool it looks."

00:12:22.841 --> 00:12:24.910
-Yeah.
-It also gives you diarrhea.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.579
-Yeah.
-Most cool things do.

00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:28.680
-Yeah, I think
if there's any message

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.282
we give to the kids...
-Yeah.

00:12:30.282 --> 00:12:32.384
-What do you --
-I mean, I feel like --

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.453
and I think a lot of people
can relate to this --

00:12:34.453 --> 00:12:37.656
My For You Page,
TikTok For You Page,

00:12:37.656 --> 00:12:39.324
really does tell me
where I am, mentally.

00:12:39.324 --> 00:12:41.326
-Oh, like, mentally.
And what does it currently --

00:12:41.326 --> 00:12:45.564
-Right now there's a lot of,
like, sad stuff right now.

00:12:45.564 --> 00:12:48.233
I got -- I got to put
a little pep in my step.

00:12:48.233 --> 00:12:52.004
I can tell that I'm low-level
depressed by the fact

00:12:52.004 --> 00:12:56.475
that I'm watching too much
TikToks of, like, you know,

00:12:56.475 --> 00:13:00.713
soldiers and their, like, dogs
they've lost in war and stuff.

00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:02.848
And I'm like I need
to get back to some...

00:13:02.848 --> 00:13:03.982
-Yeah.
-...honey.

00:13:03.982 --> 00:13:05.784
-I wasn't watching it
on TikTok,

00:13:05.784 --> 00:13:08.420
but I feel like this would be
something you'd love.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:11.123
The best thing that happened
in the Olympics

00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:12.825
was watching families watch...

00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:14.426
-Oh my God. Incredible.

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:17.363
-I mean, the best.
-Incredible.

00:13:17.363 --> 00:13:19.865
-It's weird to realize,
like, I'm now --

00:13:19.865 --> 00:13:22.033
I feel bad
for the actual athlete

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:23.435
who's doing all this work,

00:13:23.435 --> 00:13:25.804
and yet I want to watch
the people watch the athlete.

00:13:25.804 --> 00:13:29.641
-And I know that there must
have been such a sad moment

00:13:29.641 --> 00:13:33.145
when the families couldn't
be there in person to see.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:34.546
I can't imagine.

00:13:34.546 --> 00:13:37.283
But to watch, like,
the Hmong community,

00:13:37.283 --> 00:13:39.050
Suni Lee's family together,

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:41.620
who, like, supported
her gymnastics

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.555
and they got to be together?

00:13:43.555 --> 00:13:46.425
Like, being in that crowd.
That must have been...

00:13:46.425 --> 00:13:49.061
-And there was the swimmer
from Alaska, the same thing.

00:13:49.061 --> 00:13:51.030
Just, you know, the community.
-Yeah.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:55.467
-Also it's really fun
to watch people, like --

00:13:55.467 --> 00:13:59.437
like, a group of people that are
pounding and urging someone on.

00:13:59.437 --> 00:14:00.906
-Yeah.
-You've seen this.

00:14:00.906 --> 00:14:04.376
There's a lot of talk about
celebrities not taking showers.

00:14:04.376 --> 00:14:05.911
-Oh, yeah.
-Have you been following this?

00:14:05.911 --> 00:14:07.980
-Yeah, I have seen that.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:10.082
-Gyllenhaal not showering a lot.

00:14:10.082 --> 00:14:13.018
Dwayne Johnson has come out --
three showers a day.

00:14:13.018 --> 00:14:14.320
-Three a day?
-Yeah.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:15.820
-Well.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.090
I mean, it's a lot of body
to wash on DJ.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:22.327
-Lotta Rock.
-Lotta Rock. Um...

00:14:22.327 --> 00:14:25.331
I feel like I want to get
Judge Judy's take on that.

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:26.765
-Okay.

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:28.867
-I feel like whatever Judge
Judy says I would agree with.

00:14:28.867 --> 00:14:31.403
-You would just cede
the decision.

00:14:31.403 --> 00:14:33.672
-Yeah. I always agree with
her decisions for the most part.

00:14:33.672 --> 00:14:36.641
But if she said,
"What? Like, who cares?

00:14:36.641 --> 00:14:39.144
Like, shower whenever you want."
I'd be like, "Of course."

00:14:39.144 --> 00:14:42.514
And then if she said, "Shower
every day, ya crazy person."

00:14:42.514 --> 00:14:44.350
You know, I'd be like,
"Judy's right."

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.151
So I don't have a strong --
I don't have a strong opinion.

00:14:46.151 --> 00:14:49.721
-What do you think
Judy would say if, um...

00:14:49.721 --> 00:14:51.457
Cuomo touched her stomach?

00:14:51.457 --> 00:14:54.192
[ Laughter ]

00:14:54.192 --> 00:14:56.061
Do a Judge Judy for me
as Cuomo touching her stomach.

00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.963
-I'll tell you something
about Judge Judy that I think

00:14:57.963 --> 00:14:59.865
she would want everyone
to be reminded of.

00:14:59.865 --> 00:15:01.767
She keeps it tight.
-Yeah.

00:15:01.767 --> 00:15:05.103
-So her stomach is incredible!

00:15:05.103 --> 00:15:07.172
Whoever's touching it.

00:15:07.172 --> 00:15:11.410
She has the cutest
little chassis!

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:15.280
Judy looks --
Judy, you look fantastic!

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.316
And I don't know
what she's doing.

00:15:17.316 --> 00:15:20.519
But, damn, she keeps it tight.
That's neither here nor there.

00:15:20.519 --> 00:15:25.323
But what would she do
if Cuomo -- Oh, boy.

00:15:25.323 --> 00:15:28.093
This feels like a fun short film
we can make.

00:15:28.093 --> 00:15:30.529
[ Laughter ]

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:34.199
I don't know. Probably be like,
um, "What are you, nuts?"

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:37.135
-I think she would just, like,
hit him back in the stomach.

00:15:37.135 --> 00:15:39.905
-Yep. Yep.
Or maybe she would have a gavel.

00:15:39.905 --> 00:15:41.640
-Oh, a gavel.
-She'd gavel him.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.642
She'd get him right -- She'd
get him right in the gavel.

00:15:43.642 --> 00:15:46.745
-She'd wait until his hand
went back on a hard surface.

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:48.313
-And then she'd gavel the hand.

00:15:48.313 --> 00:15:49.782
[ Laughter ]

00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:52.150
Either way --
Either way he would owe her

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:55.053
$250 for legal fees.
-Right.

00:15:55.053 --> 00:15:56.988
Well, I think, if anything,
we've really put a bow

00:15:56.988 --> 00:15:59.057
on the Andrew Cuomo
governorship.

00:15:59.057 --> 00:16:01.326
-Yep. Well, what a day.
What a day for him.

00:16:01.326 --> 00:16:03.628
And thank you.
You know, you guys are always

00:16:03.628 --> 00:16:05.831
doing your great jokes here,
and they're always great.

00:16:05.831 --> 00:16:07.566
But, I mean,
wasn't this exciting

00:16:07.566 --> 00:16:09.501
